  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n The\n Five\n Liberations of\n Wisdom from\n the\n Dominion of Falsity\n\n\n---\n\n\n**\n¶1:**\n There\n are five stages of liberation by which wisdom\n is\n recovered from all the dominions and\n governing\n powers of falsity and\n evil.\n\n**¶2:**\n The first loos\nening and recovery is that of the celest\nial mind itself. For\n when the primordial divine\n understanding\n was\n delivered from its\n captivity under the rule\n of falsities by the proceeding divine\n life—\nwhich\n had come forth\n toward\n it\n—\nan immense\n measure\n of wisdom and spiritual power was recovered from\n the entire government of evil. These asc\nended together with the celestial mind into\n the heavenly degrees of\n the Lord\n's kingdom\n. This is the first liberation.\n\n\n**¶3:** The second recovery\n is that accomplished\n through the proceeding divine life. For\n when Divine Love and Divine Wisdom together\n formed the interior degrees\n and\n the exterior natural states of\n the mind—and\n brought\n order to the natural\n states and the\n false\n persu\nasions ruling\n within\n them\n—an immeas\nurable portion of wisdom was recovered from these\n:\n all\n that\n the\n celest\nial mind had yiel\nded up\n when\n it was\n consumed\n by the\n assault\n of falsity…\n\n\n**¶4:** \n*(\nThe\n text is largely\n lost\n here.)\n* …\nthrough\n three\n states of spiritual combat…\n extending\n to\n the time\n when…\n above\n… them upon…\n the whole\n order of the mind.\n\n**\n¶5:** The third recovery is that\n of the Divine Truth proceeding further\n into the rational\n degree. It\n made\n visible\n the\n form of heavenly wisdom…\n before the governing\n power\n of falsity… and recovered wisdom from\n it. This,\n then\n, is how the form of divine truth\n is\n made\n manifest through\n this further proceeding into\n the lower understanding\n.\n\n**¶6:** The\n fourth recovery is that of Divine Truth itself\n revealed\n in its full splendor. For\n when it was made manifest within\n the sphere of spiritual life, it displayed\n the form of heavenly wisdom before the\n fixed structures of the understanding and\n purified all\n the\n wisdom dwelling in the higher degrees. It\n brought order to the natural states of\n mind\n and all the bonds and\n attach\nments holding them in\n place. It also released wisdom beyond measure\n throughout the entire structure of the regener\nating mind. It gave the calling\n-\nforth of truth and the capacity of willing\n reception to the fundamental faculties,\n and from these it\n formed a new interior will—\na\n new love\n of good\n born\n within\n truth\n.\n It then ascended and came to rest\n in the celestial state.\n\n**\n¶7:** The fifth liberation\n and\n recovery is that of\n divine\n providence working\n as\n a\n whole\n—\nwhich is the calling-\nforth of truth and the\n responsive\n reception by the will—since this,\n too, recovers the interior spiritual life\n from out\n of the heav\nenly degrees and\n carries\n it into its\n final embod\niment.\n\n**¶8:**\n *(Much\n is\n lost.)\n* …the\n proceeding divine life… as it accomplished\n each\n liberation… The first… ascended…\n wisdom… The fourth… its wisdom…\n And also the\n fifth… enters into the\n whole\n and\n brings all into final order… the form\n of wisdom made visible in this ultimate containing\n vessel—the Last Form in which all\n recovered good is gathered\n and\n embodied.\n\n**¶9\n:** These\n five great powers of liberation were made manifest\n. They came to their increase\n and\n fruition;\n they were established upon the foundation\n of…\n the celestial mind… when it came\n forth from spiritual combat. It brought order\n to and built up the whole structure of\n the mind…\n the celestial mind… through\n its\n advent\n into\n the world.\n\n**¶10\n:** In\n this way they\n stand together in\n their\n ordering\n…\n\n**¶11:** …\nbecause of the wisdom that had rushed\n forth from… the proceeding Divine\n Truth in\n the\n rational\n degree.\n\n\n**¶12:** The governance\n of divine providence—which is the calling\n-forth of truth and its\n reception by the will—shall accomplish its\n final work. In this last state of\n spiritual development, it\n shall bring life to the ultimate Form,\n and that\n Form shall judge all interior spiritual states and\n shall\n send forth its\n powers.\n It is alive according to the will of\n the Divine Father, the One\n who is established and all\n-powerful.\n They go forth against evil;\n they overcome\n all of it\n; they conquer the natural mind in\n which\n they had\n lab\nored forever\n. For\n they came forth from Him in the beginning\n, even\n as they shall return again into\n wisdom. They ascend to Him at\n the last.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "reconstructed_text": "[There are] five [releases by] which the light is saved f[rom] all [the rulers and] powers of darkness!"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[The first loo]sening and saving is that of [the] First Man, since when the First M[a]n was freed fro[m the prison of] the rulers by the Living Spirit, who had come [forth to the aid] of the First Man, much light and [much] power was saved from the entire ruling-power. They ascended with the First Man to the aeons [of] greatn[ess]. This [is the first] release."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "The second saving is that of the Liv[ing] Spirit, since whe[n] the Father of Life and [the] Mother of [Li]fe constructed [the heavens] and [w]orlds [and set in order the wo]rlds, the earths and their [rulers; im]measurable light was saved f[r]om them [, all that the First] Man, who w[a]s devoured [by the darkness, had lost of his] lig[ht and power.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And there were] [also] three wars [that were waged,] to the time when he [was raised up] above [all of] them upon the [whole] universe."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Th]e fourth s[av]ing is that of Jesus the Splendour, since whe[n he was] re[ve]aled in the zone he displayed [his im]age in front of the firmaments and purified [the light] that is above. He took the likeness [of the powers, and] he made himself like the angels in [every aeon,] un[til] he travelled and descended to the form of flesh. He set in order [t]he earths and all the fastenings. He also loosen[ed and saved] light without measure in the entire structure. He gave [the] summons and the obedience to the elements, he formed [J]esus the Youth. He as[ce]n[d]ed and rested himself in the light [land]."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "The fifth release and saving is that of the great counsel, w[hich is the s]umm[ons an]d the obedience, since it also [sends forth] the soul from the [land] of greatness."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And] the Living Spirit [accomplished his work,] as he gave [forth] the release [of the light in each.] The first [power rose; he] ascended and he [saved the light,] as he [brought forth] wisdom [from the darkness.] The fourth [also brought forth] its wisdom [in like manner.] And also, the fifth [enters] into it, and it sets it in order [and manifests] its light image in this Last Statue."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 10,
      "reconstructed_text": "In [t]his way [also] they st[an]d with [one another in their ordering.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 11,
      "reconstructed_text": "[And this is] because of the light [th]at had rushed from [the image of] the Amba[s]sa[d]or."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "These five grea[\nt] powe[rs of the\n light] were revealed. They came to\n a profit [and a gain, and\n] they were established upon [the foundation\n of the] First Man [who arose\n] when he came to/ward [\nthe heights] from the struggle. He\n set in order and constructed [the whole\n] universe [through] the First M\n[an at] his advent."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[The third red]emption is that of the Thi[rd Ambassador ... he] displayed [his image ...] he [... ... the r]uling-power; he [... ... ... ...] from them [... ...] So this is [how] the [...] his image that [...] in the Th[ir]d Ambassador."
    }
